            <ArticleTitle>An unusual cause of intractable secondary dysmenorrhea.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1058-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Severe dysmenorrhea following sterilization may be due to the presence of a noncommunicating horn of a bicornuate uterus. Ultrasound examination should be made before a functional basis is considered for such pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
